# Testing Standards

## Core Testing Principles

1. **Test before deploy** — every workflow must pass test scenarios before going live
2. **Pin test data** — external data nodes must have pinned test data
3. **Test the sad path** — error scenarios are as important as happy path
4. **Isolate external calls** — use pinned data to avoid hitting live services during testing
5. **Deterministic tests** — test scenarios must produce the same result every run

## Test Scenario Structure

Every workflow spec must include test scenarios covering:

```markdown
## Test Scenarios

### Happy Path
- Input: (exact data structure)
- Expected output: (exact fields and values)
- Expected side effects: (notifications sent, DB records created, etc.)

### Edge Cases
- Empty input: what happens with null or empty data
- Partial data: required fields missing
- Boundary values: max/min sizes, date edge cases

### Error Scenarios
- External service unavailable: expected notification and graceful exit
- Invalid input: expected validation error and response
- Auth failure: expected credential error handling
```

## Pinned Test Data Rules

- Required on ALL nodes that fetch external data (HTTP Request, DB query, API node)
- Must represent realistic data shapes — no placeholder strings like "test" or "123"
- Must include at least one edge case (empty array, null field, max-length string)
- Never use production data as pinned test data (PII concern)

## Manual Test Checklist

Before every deployment, verify:

- [ ] Happy path executed successfully end-to-end
- [ ] Error Trigger fires correctly on simulated failure
- [ ] No sensitive data appears in execution logs
- [ ] Notification nodes send correctly formatted messages
- [ ] Idempotency: running workflow twice produces no duplicate side effects
- [ ] All IF/Switch branches have been exercised at least once

## AI Agent Testing

When testing workflows with AI Agent nodes:

- Pin sample outputs that represent the agent's expected response format
- Test with inputs that should trigger the fallback/error path
- Verify output validation node correctly rejects malformed agent responses
- Test with boundary inputs (very long text, special characters, empty strings)
